# Linear Issue Curator (automation 1 of 2)

Read `.cursor/skills/linear-curator.md` before running. Each run **maintains** the existing `suggestion` issues, then **discovers** new ones — all **in Linear**, never GitHub.

Key points:
- **Issues live in Linear. Never create a GitHub issue.** Create/update via the `LINEAR_API_KEY` against the Linear GraphQL API (auth, helper, ID cache in `docs/internal/ci-cd/CURSOR_AUTOMATIONS.md`). Transport-agnostic — if a Linear MCP is available in your environment, use it instead of the GraphQL API; the write just needs to land in Linear.
- **Ownership boundary (hard rule):** only ever cancel / relabel / re-body / comment / set-priority on issues carrying the `suggestion` label. Every other issue (epics, Projects, human-filed) is READ-ONLY. Run the pre-write label gate (read the issue's labels) before any write.
- **Maintenance first:** set **Done** for suggestions the code/spec *proves* resolved, **Canceled** for obsolete/duplicate (with a `duplicate` relation), refresh drifted descriptions, add `stale` (don't close) when you can't prove resolution. Close only what you can cite.
- **Read-only on code** — issues only. Never edit files, push branches, or open PRs.
- **Conservative net-new budget:** prefer refreshing a near-match; cap ~3 net-new (tighter when the backlog is large) to keep the Backlog lean for signal quality. A cap guard files nothing only when **active** (Started+Unstarted) nears Linear's 250 limit — Backlog/archived don't count, so it rarely binds. Zero new issues is valid.
- New issues are created in the **Triage** state with `suggestion` + one `area:<x>` label, a **Priority** set, optional `projectId`, the standard description template, and a hidden `fp=<area>/<slug>` dedup marker. Don't do triage's job — `linear-triage.md` prioritizes/buckets/promotes.
